# pixi environments
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml

# pixi build/publish output -- `pixi build` writes the built package
# directly into the current directory by default
*.conda

# generated example output
examples/*.bmp
examples/*.png
examples/*.svg

# generated test artifacts
tests/_test_*.bmp
tests/_test_*.png
tests/_test_*.svg

# modo doc-generator binary (scripts/install-modo.sh) and its
# `mojo doc` JSON input -- regenerated by `pixi run docs`, not
# committed.
.tools/
docs/src/*.json

# docs/src/examples/ is entirely generated -- the .md pages by
# scripts/gen_example_docs.mojo (from examples/*.mojo's own
# docstrings/source), the images copied from examples/out_*.bmp|png
# (themselves generated by `pixi run example`). docs/src/_index.md
# (the landing page) and docs/src/api-guide/ (the API overview) are
# real hand-written source. Modo's own generated Hugo content and
# Hugo's own built static site are generated too, from docs/src/ --
# none of this is committed; all of it is deployed straight to GitHub
# Pages by .github/workflows/docs.yml's own Actions-based deploy,
# regenerated fresh on every run. docs/site/'s own Hugo *project*
# files (hugo.yaml, go.mod/go.sum, layouts/) ARE committed -- those
# are real source, not output. So is docs/hero.svg, README.md's own
# hero image -- see that file's own comment for why.
docs/src/examples/
docs/site/content/
docs/site/public/
docs/site/*.lock

# tests/consumer/ is a downstream workspace that builds canvas_mojo as
# a package and imports it (see its own pixi.toml). Its .pixi/ ignores
# itself; this is the rest of what running it leaves behind.
#
# Its lock is deliberately not committed, unlike the root pixi.lock:
# the lock records the dependency by source hash
# (`canvas_mojo[<hash>] @ ../..`), which changes on every edit under
# canvas/, so a committed one would go stale with each change to the
# library. Resolving fresh is also what an actual downstream user does.
tests/consumer/pixi.lock
tests/consumer/smoke_out.*

# Agent worktrees created by Claude Code (see .claude/), never part of
# the project itself.
.claude/worktrees/
